---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What ReaderTweaks is, how the guides are made, and how the site pays for itself."
  path="/about/"
  activeNav="about"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
  ])}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>ReaderTweaks</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A practical reference for getting more out of e-ink readers — organised by
        the exact device you own.
      </p>

      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Every e-reader has a permanent hub here, and under each one the same seven
        sections: Guides, KOReader, Calibre, Customization, Troubleshooting,
        Accessories and Comparisons. The aim is that when you search for a
        specific problem on a specific device, the page you land on is written for
        that device and nothing else.
      </p>

      <h2>How the guides are made</h2>
      <p>
        Steps are walked through on the actual hardware and dated. E-reader
        firmware changes often, so when a step depends on a firmware version the
        page says which one. If something here is wrong or out of date, that is a
        bug — see contact below.
      </p>

      <h2 id="disclosure">Affiliate disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Some links to accessories are affiliate links. If you buy through one,
        ReaderTweaks may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. It does
        not change which products get recommended — picks are based on fit and
        reliability, not commission.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections and suggestions: <a href="mailto:hello@readertweaks.com">hello@readertweaks.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        ReaderTweaks is independent and not affiliated with Kobo, Amazon, Onyx,
        PocketBook, reMarkable or any other manufacturer. Product names are used
        for identification only.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
</style>
